  "[{\"document_id\":\":behavioral-subtree:#uuid \\\"0f11dba5-c331-3cdf-81fa-8ee114fc224f\\\"\",\"reasoning\":\"The user is asking to evaluate a specific artifact (an excerpt from a vendor agreement) against quality/risk criteria and identify issues. This matches the 'Critique' behavior, which specifically produces 'located issues + suggested fixes' and recommends adversarial framing (safety auditor) or an explicit checklist, exactly what is needed to flag risks in a contract before signing.\",\"fitness_score\":1.0,\"domain_reasoning\":\"The task involves evaluating a legal agreement for risks/issues. Critique's representative use of 'evaluates an artifact against quality criteria, producing... located issues' covers the material (agreement excerpt) and output kind (flagged issues).\",\"domain_coverage\":\"covered\",\"domain_label\":\"contract-risk-analysis\"},{\"document_id\":\":behavioral-subtree:#uuid \\\"1361eafc-6a90-391a-97a9-b558118f1f57\\\"\",\"reasoning\":\"Validation checks against formal rules producing pass/fail. While this task has elements of checking rules (indemnity/subcontracting policies), the query asks 'What issues should I flag?', which implies a degree of judgment and qualitative risk assessment rather than a simple boolean pass/fail against a schema. The 'avoid-when' for validation suggests using 'Critique' for judgment-based quality assessment.\",\"fitness_score\":0.7,\"domain_reasoning\":\"Matches the 'checking against rules' aspect of legal compliance, but the output kind 'issues to flag' is better served by Critique than formal Validation's pass/fail.\",\"domain_coverage\":\"partial\",\"domain_label\":\"contract-risk-analysis\"},{\"document_id\":\":behavioral-subtree:#uuid \\\"2bce84a1-d186-3892-8131-c19b59e4543e\\\"\",\"reasoning\":\"The user is looking at two different sections (4.2 and 7.1) and seeking a cohesive set of issues. Synthesis is useful for integrating multiple inputs, but it typically 'avoids when the task is critique (check